              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पटः — paṭaḥ — \"a cloth\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "paṭa \"woven cloth, a garment\" is probably borrowed from Austroasiatic: CDIAL 7692 follows Przyluski in grouping it with karpāsa \"cotton\", and thinks a Dravidian source less likely. Pali kept it as paṭa \"cloth\" (CDIAL 7692)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
